  "details": "<p>Enirgalana was rebuilt by the Assyrian kings Esarhaddon and Ashurbanipal. Although Eanna has been excavated, there is insufficient evidence to precisely locate\u00a0Enirgalana within the temple complex.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The cella/shrine of the goddess I\u0161tar in the Eanna temple at Uruk. The Sumerian ceremonial name Enirgalana means \"House of the Prince of Heaven.\"",
